            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "John Chung",
                        "email": "john.chung@arm.com",
                        "username": "gtossk2"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the patch. However, I think we should continue using linux-yocto to avoid any compatibility issues with the FVP model.\n\nIn addition, linux-yocto has already been validated with the FVP model and will be updated through the meta layers, so we don't need to manually track or update the revision ourselves."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Mohammed Javith Akthar M",
                        "email": "mohammedjavitham@ami.com",
                        "username": "mohammedjavitham"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the review. Using the OpenBMC kernel ensures consistency across platforms and avoids fragmentation.\n\nOther SoCs (ASPEED, Nuvoton) already follow this approach.\n- https://github.com/openbmc/openbmc/blob/master/meta-nuvoton/recipes-kernel/linux/linux-nuvoton.inc#L9\n- https://github.com/openbmc/openbmc/blob/master/meta-aspeed/recipes-kernel/linux/linux-aspeed.inc#L9\n\nWe have validated this change internally on our OpenBMC fork, and basic FVP functionalities works as intended.\n\nI recommend reconsidering this approach to keep FVP aligned with the OpenBMC strategy and reduce long-term maintenance challenges."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "John Chung",
                        "email": "john.chung@arm.com",
                        "username": "gtossk2"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the recommendation. I still think it is better to keep it simple, and using the OpenBMC kernel does not reduce the maintenance burden. For example, each time a new version of the FVP model is released, you would need to verify the system and ensure the required features are included from the Yocto kernel - something we can avoid and had verified new FVP model with the Yocto kernel."
                }
            ],
